which is very different than a currency,

00:12:45.755 --> 00:12:47.840
but that's what people
call cryptocurrencies.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:51.730
And maybe, Jim, maybe you've studied
some of these ICOs, I have no idea.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:55.573
Someone gives you cloud services or
you invest in services, that's one type.

00:12:55.573 --> 00:13:00.004
The second type you can use
cryptocurrency for fiat currency.

00:13:00.004 --> 00:13:04.330
Well, that works because it just uses
different technology to move money around.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:07.250
Basically we keep your money digitally
anyway, and if you just keep

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:11.860
different files in a different way and
distributed ledgers, that would work fine.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:15.490
But I've always thought about Bitcoin
as a currency and a store value and

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:20.670
a payment mechanism is that governments,
and this is my belief and I'm maybe wrong.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.795
I'm not telling you you
can't go to $100,000.

00:13:22.795 --> 00:13:27.630
That governments are going to crush
it one day for three reasons, okay?

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:30.660
One is when it's used for
terrorist activities, okay?

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.900
It'll happen, it's a matter of time,
it'll go back to a Bitcoin and

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:36.550
then all of a sudden, the DOJ,
the United State government,

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:40.680
all these people in Washington who
profess to love technology and

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:43.170
the novelty of Bitcoin
are going to change their mind.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.256
Number two, when a lotta little
old ladies lose their money.

00:13:45.256 --> 00:13:49.024
Because the speculative vehicle is allowed
to exist by the United States government.

00:13:49.024 --> 00:13:51.596
And they're going to lose their money,
they're going to be pounding.

00:13:51.596 --> 00:13:53.520
You should of done something about it.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.798
And number three is the most important.

00:13:54.798 --> 00:13:56.878
Whenever a government forms itself,

00:13:56.878 --> 00:14:01.233
and you go to any country in the world,
pull out the currency, look at the date,

00:14:01.233 --> 00:14:05.206
that fiat currency was formed by that
government with the central bank.

00:14:05.206 --> 00:14:07.281
Because governments like
to control their currency.

00:14:07.281 --> 00:14:11.631
They like to know who has it, where it's
going, why it's going, when it went, etc.,

00:14:11.631 --> 00:14:13.570
and right now, Bitcoin's a novelty.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:17.470
It's $100 billion and
$1 billion a day trades hands.

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:19.920
Obviously, mostly speculation, okay?

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.950
And obviously, there's a real use case,
I'm not making it as a joke.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:28.408
Venezuela, Cuba, North Korea, criminal,
drug money, that will always be true.

00:14:28.408 --> 00:14:32.976
So we'll always have a use case that's
valuable to someone because it's better in

00:14:32.976 --> 00:14:36.498
those countries to have that than
currency or money in the bank,

00:14:36.498 --> 00:14:39.125
because the governments,
they take that too.

00:14:39.125 --> 00:14:42.563
And if you go to Argentina,
they had effectively savings accounts,

00:14:42.563 --> 00:14:44.588
the government just went in and took it.

00:14:44.588 --> 00:14:49.466
They just took it, and of course, everyone
took their money out of the bank right

00:14:49.466 --> 00:14:52.650
after that, and
the country basically collapsed.

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:54.030
So that's the reason why.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.016
It's going to get bigger and bigger and
they're going to want to control it.

00:14:56.016 --> 00:14:58.385
And it's not the same as a fiat currency.

00:14:58.385 --> 00:15:02.570
A fiat currency, the government says,
you must take this as legal tender.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:10.000
And at par, effectively cash,
at par, and it's always worth par.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:14.359
And I don't know why a crypto dollar would
ever be something that the store value

00:15:14.359 --> 00:15:16.452
would be worse than a crypto Bitcoin.

00:15:16.452 --> 00:15:21.227
So that's my view and
I may be wrong, which I doubt, but-

00:15:21.227 --> 00:15:24.980
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.320
&gt;&gt; I've been wrong before, though.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.055
So, and if I'm wrong,
I also don't care very much.

00:15:29.055 --> 00:15:31.215
It'll never affect my life.

00:15:31.215 --> 00:15:34.270
It's not because they're right, or
the bankers are defending their stuff.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:36.050
Absolutely untrue.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.856
If Bitcoin works and we have to do
something, Bitcoin will do that too.

00:15:38.856 --> 00:15:40.422
&gt;&gt; Kind of a win-win there.

